# Architecture

- `block/entity`: `DreamTableBlockEntity` keeps one `TableSession` per player (a map by UUID), ticks them, saves them, and syncs them. A session holds everything a player does at the table: page, chosen farm, delivered items, placement, and build. It is built from `MaterialLedger` (delivered and used counts, swaps), `BuildProgress` (phase, step, timer, owner, speed, placed and paid steps), and `FarmPlacement` (anchor and facing).
- `writeNbt` saves everything; `toInitialChunkDataNbt` sends clients only `TableSession.writeForClient` (no slot inventory, step records, timer or signature). Data a client draws must be added there too.
- Imported schematics are parsed through `ImportedStructures`' cache (by file time and size), and `FarmTemplates` swaps in the whole new list at once. Don't fill shared lists in place.
- Never store per-player state on the table itself, and never read another player's session. Server code gets the session from the acting player; client code uses `table.session(localPlayer)`. Never cache a session on the client: each sync replaces the client's copy.
- The farm code (`FarmBuilder`, `FarmDismantler`, `FarmSpawns`) takes a `TableSession`, never the table.
- `farm`:
  - `FarmBuilder` places one step per call.
  - `FarmDismantler` takes an unfinished build apart on discard.
  - `ObstacleRules` decides what may be cleared.
  - `FarmSpawns` handles mobs and buckets.
  - `MaterialSwaps` lists compatible blocks.
- `farm/schematic`: one reader per format (`VanillaReader`, `SpongeReader`, `LitematicaReader`), driven by `SchematicReader`.
- `farm/legacy`: code-built farms, used only when a bundled `.schem` can't be read.
- `screen`: `DreamTableScreen` only wires things together. `TableButtons` is the server side of every button. Page and button ids are constants in `DreamTableScreenHandler`.
- `screen/page`: one `TablePage` per menu page. `ProjectState` reads the synced phase on the client.
- `screen/ui`: `Theme`, `Painter`, `Viewport`, `SearchBox`.
- `client/clipboard` and `client/hologram`: the world-space board and the ghost blocks.

## Server owns the state
The client only previews with `handler.preview(...)` and sends a button id. `TableButtons` changes the table, and the table calls `sync()`.

## Adding a menu page
1. Add `PAGE_*` and `BUTTON_*` constants in `DreamTableScreenHandler`.
2. Handle the buttons in `TableButtons`.
3. Create a `TablePage` in `screen/page` that draws through `PageContext` (`card`, `button`, `go`).
4. Register the page in `DreamTableScreen.page()`.
